    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0355" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.48/119: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Carroll</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d248-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-12T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 12,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 16—1:01
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>33. Alluding today to the contents of the Department’s telegram no. 6, February
                    6, 3 p.m. The Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs <pb facs="0356" n="258"
                        xml:id="pg258"/> informed me that his Government feels that its attitude
                    towards Austria has been unintentionally misrepresented and that it is now
                    preparing a statement of its position which, upon completion, he will submit to
                    me for transmission to the Department. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carroll</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d248-f1" n="7" type="source" xml:id="d248-f1-content">
